   1	/**
   2	 * Centralized error hierarchy for OpenVera.
   3	 *
   4	 * Every domain error extends {@link VeraError} and carries a machine-readable
   5	 * `code` string.  Callers that need to distinguish error categories can use
   6	 * `instanceof` checks or switch on `error.code`.
   7	 *
   8	 * Guidelines:
   9	 * - Never throw raw `Error` from library code; use one of the subclasses below.
  10	 * - Use `cause` (ES 2022 Error.cause) to preserve the original exception when
  11	 *   wrapping.
  12	 * - Keep messages human-readable; codes are for machines.
  13	 */
  14	
  15	// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
